From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amphoze <184834775+Amphoze@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] guard: no route without a verified assertion and a project
 context

The first request middleware, ahead of every other: it covers route handlers, server
functions and pages. A request whose assertion does not verify is answered 401. The path is
read with the router's own decoder and matcher, and it is the path the server hands a
middleware, not the request's URL: a route that is not served (under /api/ai, at /api/mcp)
and a segment with the shape of a ref that is not the assertion's project are answered 404,
in any letter case; a path under /api that matches no route with a handler is answered 404,
and 405 with Allow when the route has no handler for the method. What passes runs inside
the context of the assertion's project, as the control plane answers for it; a refusal of
the control plane, or one thrown further down, is the answer {code, message}.

The build's prerender starts the server once without a node's settings and asks for the
application shell. In that mode, which is the process's environment and nothing a request
carries, one kind of request passes: a GET with the shell's header and no assertion for a
page - no API path, no server function, no route with a server handler. A process that has
the switch and any setting of a node stops.
